 Card (RFC 9553), e.g. `name.full`, `nicknames`, `speakToAs.pronouns`. Absent: a vendor-specific property named by the key."},"required":{"type":"boolean"},"ceiling":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Audience"},"defaultVisibility":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Audience"},"searchable":{"type":"boolean"},"facet":{"type":"boolean"},"order":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10000},"state":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/FieldState"},"retiredAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the field was retired. Present only on a retired field."},"purgeAfter":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the values of a retired field are purged. Present only on a retired field."},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"ext":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Ext","description":"Ecosystem-defined extension members per SPEC.md §4.5.1. An extension member MUST NOT widen a ceiling."}}},"FieldState":{"title":"FieldState","description":"`active`: in use. `disabled`: a base field the community has switched off; hidden from every projection and re-enablable. `retired`: a community field withdrawn for good; hidden at once, its values purged after the community\'s retention period, and its key never reused.","type":"string","enum":["active","disabled","retired"]},"FieldSource":{"title":"FieldSource","description":"Who writes the value. `member`: self-asserted, through vtc/directory/card/update. `admin`: asserted by the community through vtc/directory/card/assert; the member reads it and cannot change it. `credential`: a claim the member discloses from a credential through vtc/directory/card/present, badged with its issuer. `derived`: a base field read from the community\'s own records (`role`, `joinedAt`, `did`, `personhood`) and never stored on a card. Each source is written only through its own path.","type":"string","enum":["member","admin","credential","derived"]},"FieldConstraints":{"title":"FieldConstraints","description":"Per-type constraints. A member that does not apply to the field\'s type is refused by the community with `valueInvalid` when the definition is written.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"maxLength":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":2000},"minLength":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2000},"pattern":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"description":"ECMA-262 regular expression a text value MUST match."},"options":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":128,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EnumOption"},"description":"The permitted values of an `enum` or `multiEnum` field."},"maxItems":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":32},"minDate":{"type":"string","format":"date"},"maxDate":{"type":"string","format":"date"},"claim":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ClaimSelector"}}},"ClaimSelector":{"title":"ClaimSelector","description":"Which claim a `claim` field accepts, from which credentials and issuers.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["credentialType","claimPath"],"properties":{"credentialType":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"A `type` the presented credential MUST carry."},"claimPath":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":256,"description":"JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) to the claim within `credentialSubject`."},"issuers":{"type":"array","maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","maxLength":2048},"description":"Issuers the community accepts for this field. Absent: the community\'s trusted issuers for the credential type, as its own policy decides."}}},"EnumOption":{"title":"EnumOption","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["value","label"],"properties":{"value":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._-]{0,63}\$","description":"The stored value."},"label":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"What a reader is shown for it."}}},"FieldType":{"title":"FieldType","description":"The kind of value a field holds, which fixes its `FieldValue` shape. `did` holds a DID the member chooses to show (never their membership DID, which is the derived base field `did`). `claim` holds a `VerifiedValue` and requires `source: credential`.","type":"string","enum":["text","longText","url","email","phone","enum","multiEnum","date","country","image","did","claim"]},"FieldDescription":{"title":"FieldDescription","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":280,"description":"Help text shown to a member filling the field in. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"FieldLabel":{"title":"FieldLabel","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"What readers see as the field\'s name. Plain text."},"Audience":{"title":"Audience","description":"Who may see a directory field, ordered from narrowest to widest. `admins`: holders of `vtc.directory.admin` (and, for derived fields, `vtc.members.manage`). `groups`: members who share at least one community group with the subject (narrowed to the groups the subject names in `groupAudience`, where it names any). `connections`: members holding an attributed, in-force verified relationship with the subject at the community. `members`: every active member. `public`: anyone, and what the member\'s signed public card carries outside the community.\\n\\n`groups` and `connections` are not a chain: a viewer sees a field when they satisfy the audience the subject chose for it or any wider audience. Every audience includes the administrators, and the subject always sees their own whole card. There is no `onlyMe`: a value nobody else should see is not directory data.","type":"string","enum":["admins","groups","connections","members","public"]},"FieldKey":{"title":"FieldKey","description":"Identifier of a directory field. A key with no `.` is a BASE field, the same in every community: `displayName`, `nickname`, `avatar`, `pronouns`, `bio`, `links` (written by the member) and `role`, `joinedAt`, `did`, `personhood` (derived from the community\'s own records, never stored on